# Overview
#
# `due to the fact that` spends five words on what `because` says in one
# (`It failed due to the fact that the disk was full`). The fix writes
# `because`. The rule sits at Required, because it matches one exact
# phrase and the fix is mechanical.
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Required ProseWordy reports the other stock phrases that have a
# one-word form, such as `owing to the fact that`. It leaves `due to the
# fact that` to this rule, which carries the rewrite to `because`.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule did not hit any line in the measure.py corpus, so no sample
# measures its precision.
expr main due to the fact that
let message "`due to the fact that`. Write `because`."
let description "Shortens `due to the fact that`."
let becomes "because"
let kind "Style"
test "It failed due to the fact that the disk was full." "It failed because the disk was full."
allows "It failed because the disk was full."
